To return a custom status code from a path operation, you can return a Response directly, like a JSONResponse, and set the status_code that you want. For example, you can use `status.HTTP_201_CREATED` or `status.HTTP_404_NOT_FOUND`. 

```python
from fastapi import status
from fastapi.responses import JSONResponse

@app.put("/items/{item_id}")
async def upsert_item(
    item_id: str,
    name: Annotated[str | None, Body()] = None,
    size: Annotated[int | None, Body()] = None,
):
    if item_id in items:
        item = items[item_id]
        item["name"] = name
        item["size"] = size
        return item
    else:
        item = {"name": name, "size": size}
        items[item_id] = item
        return JSONResponse(status_code=status.HTTP_201_CREATED, content=item)
```
